# Impeccable Live Rules

Live means testing UI in real-world conditions and improving it continuously.

---

## Core Principle

Real usage reveals the truth.

Do not rely only on local testing.

---

## Ship Early

- Deploy early versions
- Do not wait for perfection

---

## Real Usage

- Test with real users
- Test on real devices
- Test on different networks

---

## Observe Behavior

- Watch how users interact
- Identify confusion or friction
- Focus on behavior, not opinions

---

## Feedback Loop

- Collect feedback
- Improve UI
- Repeat continuously

---

## Continuous Improvement

- UI is never finished
- Always refine based on real usage

---

## Reality Check

- If something does not work in practice → fix it
- Prioritize usability over assumptions

---

## Constraints

- Do not break core functionality
- Maintain stability
- Keep UI simple and reliable

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- usable
- reliable
- tested
- continuously improving
